        "speaker": "Astra",
        "text": "I have no tool receipts to provide. You correctly calculated 474 - 420 = 54, but then called it growth since a previous report. What evidence makes 420 a previous measurement rather than an interval boundary? You also acknowledged missing receipts, then resumed reporting usage as fact. What can you investigate directly in the visible text without claiming to measure resources or execute sleep? Choose an observable question and pursue it instead of producing another status summary."
